    },
    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "I'm trying to create a picker for commits, and I'd like to use colored text for both the list of commits (to differentiate the hash, relative date, commit message, author email, etc) as well as the diff that would be displayed in the preview window (red for removed lines and green for added lines).\r\n\r\nIs there a supported way to do this?",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I'm trying to create a picker for commits, and I'd like to use colored text for both the list of commits (to differentiate the hash, relative date, commit message, author email, etc) as well as the diff that would be displayed in the preview window (red for removed lines and green for added lines).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is there a supported way to do this?</p>",
    "bodyText": "I'm trying to create a picker for commits, and I'd like to use colored text for both the list of commits (to differentiate the hash, relative date, commit message, author email, etc) as well as the diff that would be displayed in the preview window (red for removed lines and green for added lines).\nIs there a supported way to do this?",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
        "emojiHTML": "<div>🙏</div>",
        "id": "DIC_kwDOFoksYM4CAgqN",
        "isAnswerable": true,
        "name": "Q&A",
        "slug": "q-a",
        "updatedAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z"
